IMPORT prelude

-- Executive Condominium Housing Scheme Act 1996 (Singapore), 2020 Revised
-- Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 December 2025.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/ECHSA1996.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill and
-- nothing else: no pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. Observations, not checked findings.
--
-- SCOPE. ss 5, 6, 7 and 9 -- who may not buy, what happens when a disqualified
-- person does, the two windows in which the accommodation may not be
-- transferred, and the grounds on which it may be compulsorily acquired.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 1-4 (short title, interpretation, the scheme itself, the
-- appointment of developers), s 8 (transmission on death), ss 10-14 (premium on
-- resale, service, immunity, the Residential Property Act and the Minister's
-- general power). The regulations under s 3(2), which carry the real
-- eligibility conditions, were not retrieved.
--
-- "Minimum occupation period" is defined by reference to what is prescribed, so
-- every rule that reads it takes "within the minimum occupation period" as a
-- fact rather than computing a date. That is also why no DATE type appears:
-- the periods in this Act are prescribed elsewhere or are fact questions.

§ `Executive Condominium Housing Scheme Act 1996`

§§ `5 -- Eligibility to purchase`

-- s 5(1): "a person is not entitled to purchase any housing accommodation under
-- the executive condominium scheme if THE PERSON OR HIS OR HER SPOUSE has at
-- any time -- (a) ... owned or purchased any flat, house, building or land ...;
-- (b) ... sold any flat ... or divested himself or herself of any estate or
-- interest therein; (c) made any misrepresentation of a material fact or false
-- statement in a material particular, WHETHER INNOCENTLY OR OTHERWISE ...; or
-- (d) ... become ineligible ... by virtue of any regulations made under
-- section 3(2)."
--
-- Every limb attaches to the person OR the spouse, so each fact is recorded for
-- the couple rather than the applicant. The windows differ between limbs and
-- are part of each fact's name:
--   (a) between application and the temporary occupation permit;
--   (b) 30 months before application, OR between application and the permit;
--   (c) no window at all;
--   (d) between application and the permit.
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `name`  IS A STRING
    -- (a)
    `the person or spouse owned or purchased property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (b), first window
    `the person or spouse sold or divested property within 30 months before the application` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (b), second window
    `the person or spouse sold or divested property between application and the temporary occupation permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (c)
    `the person or spouse made a misrepresentation of material fact or a false statement in a material particular relating to the purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (d)
    `the person or spouse became ineligible under regulations made under section 3(2) between application and the permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(9): the commercial-property saving.
    `the property concerned is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister has allowed a higher value than $250,000` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 5(9): "Nothing in subsection (1) disqualifies a person ... if the person or
-- his or her spouse has purchased or acquired, WITH THE MINISTER'S PRIOR
-- WRITTEN CONSENT, any commercial property not exceeding $250,000 in value, or
-- such higher value as the Minister may allow, at the time of purchase."
--
-- Three cumulative conditions: commercial property, prior written consent, and
-- the value cap. The cap is $250,000 unless the Minister has allowed more, and
-- whether more has been allowed is a fact.
`the commercial property value cap in dollars` MEANS 250000

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 5(9) saving applies` IF
        `the applicant`'s `the property concerned is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent`
    AND `the value is within the cap` `the applicant`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the value is within the cap` IF
        `the applicant`'s `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars`
            AT MOST `the commercial property value cap in dollars`
    OR  `the applicant`'s `the Minister has allowed a higher value than $250,000`

-- The four limbs of s 5(1), joined by "or".
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground in section 5(1) applies` IF
        `the applicant`'s `the person or spouse owned or purchased property between application and the temporary occupation permit`
    ..  `section 5(1)(b) applies` `the applicant`
    ..  `the applicant`'s `the person or spouse made a misrepresentation of material fact or a false statement in a material particular relating to the purchase`
    OR  `the applicant`'s `the person or spouse became ineligible under regulations made under section 3(2) between application and the permit`

-- (b) itself has two windows, joined by "or".
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(1)(b) applies` IF
        `the applicant`'s `the person or spouse sold or divested property within 30 months before the application`
    OR  `the applicant`'s `the person or spouse sold or divested property between application and the temporary occupation permit`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` IF
        `a ground in section 5(1) applies` `the applicant`
    AND NOT `the section 5(9) saving applies` `the applicant`

-- s 5(2): "Where any person purchases ... in contravention of subsection (1),
-- he or she must not present for registration under the Land Titles Act 1993
-- the assurance of the housing accommodation."
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser must not present the assurance for registration` IF
    `the person is not entitled to purchase under section 5(1)` `the applicant`

-- s 5(3): where, BEFORE the temporary occupation permit issues, the developer
-- is satisfied that a purchaser has contravened s 5(1) or s 7(1)(a), the
-- developer MUST serve one of two notices: (a) of intention to lodge a vesting
-- instrument, or (b) where no assurance has been registered, of intention to
-- terminate the sale and purchase agreement.
DECLARE DeveloperSituation HAS
    `the applicant`                         IS AN Applicant
    `the temporary occupation permit has issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the developer is satisfied of a contravention of section 5(1) or section 7(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an assurance has been registered in favour of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 5(4): "within 14 days after service of the notice, appeal to the
    -- Minister whose decision is final".
    `the purchaser appealed to the Minister within 14 days after service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appeal has been disposed of`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the situation` IS A DeveloperSituation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer must serve a section 5(3) notice` IF
        NOT `the situation`'s `the temporary occupation permit has issued`
    AND `the situation`'s `the developer is satisfied of a contravention of section 5(1) or section 7(1)(a)`

-- (a) or (b): which notice depends on whether an assurance has been registered.
GIVEN `the situation` IS A DeveloperSituation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is one of intention to terminate the agreement under section 5(3)(b)` IF
        `the developer must serve a section 5(3) notice` `the situation`
    AND NOT `the situation`'s `an assurance has been registered in favour of the purchaser`

GIVEN `the situation` IS A DeveloperSituation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is one of intention to lodge a vesting instrument under section 5(3)(a)` IF
        `the developer must serve a section 5(3) notice` `the situation`
    AND `the situation`'s `an assurance has been registered in favour of the purchaser`

-- s 5(5): "Where an appeal has been made to the Minister under subsection (4),
-- the developer MUST NOT proceed to lodge any instrument ... until the appeal
-- has been disposed of."
GIVEN `the situation` IS A DeveloperSituation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer must not lodge the vesting instrument yet` IF
        `the situation`'s `the purchaser appealed to the Minister within 14 days after service`
    AND NOT `the situation`'s `the appeal has been disposed of`

-- s 5(8): "The Government must, after deducting a penalty NOT EXCEEDING $10,000
-- as may be prescribed, distribute the remainder ..." A ceiling, so the rule
-- states the ceiling and the prescribed figure is a fact.
`the maximum section 5(8) penalty in dollars` MEANS 10000

§§ `6 -- Death of applicant before issue of temporary occupation permit`

-- s 6: "Where any applicant ... dies before the issue of the temporary
-- occupation permit ..., the developer MUST, UNLESS THE MINISTER OTHERWISE
-- DIRECTS, cancel the application and terminate the sale and purchase agreement
-- (if any), and all moneys paid or deposited, less any administrative and legal
-- costs reasonably incurred by the developer, must be refunded ..."
GIVEN `the applicant died before the permit issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the Minister has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the developer must cancel the application under section 6` IF
        `the applicant died before the permit issued`
    AND NOT `the Minister has otherwise directed`

GIVEN `the moneys paid or deposited` IS A NUMBER
    , `the administrative and legal costs reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount refundable under section 6` IS
    `the moneys paid or deposited` MINUS `the administrative and legal costs reasonably incurred`

§§ `7 -- Prohibition of transfers`

-- s 7(1): "EXCEPT WITH THE MINISTER'S PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT, a person must
-- not -- (a) between the date an application to purchase ... is made ... and the
-- date of issue of the temporary occupation permit ...; or (b) within the
-- minimum occupation period, transfer the housing accommodation ... or create
-- any trust for sale ..."
--
-- Two windows, one prohibition, one consent that lifts it.
DECLARE Transfer HAS
    `a transfer of the accommodation or an estate or interest, or the creation of a trust for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made between the application and the issue of the temporary occupation permit` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `made within the minimum occupation period` IS A BOOLEAN                                        -- (b)
    `the Minister gave prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer falls in a prohibited window` IF
        `the transfer`'s `made between the application and the issue of the temporary occupation permit`
    OR  `the transfer`'s `made within the minimum occupation period`

GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` IF
        `the transfer`'s `a transfer of the accommodation or an estate or interest, or the creation of a trust for sale`
    AND `the transfer falls in a prohibited window` `the transfer`
    AND NOT `the transfer`'s `the Minister gave prior written consent`

-- s 7(2): "Any transfer made or trust created in contravention of
-- subsection (1) is VOID." Not voidable, and not merely an offence: the
-- transfer does not happen at all.
GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is void under section 7(2)` IF
    `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` `the transfer`

-- s 7(3): an offence, fine not exceeding $10,000.
GIVEN `the transfer` IS A Transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 7(3)` IF
    `the transfer contravenes section 7(1)` `the transfer`

`the maximum section 7(3) fine in dollars` MEANS 10000

§§ `9 -- Compulsory acquisition`

-- s 9(1): "the Minister MAY direct the Board to compulsorily acquire the
-- housing accommodation if the Minister is satisfied that -- (a) any purchaser
-- ... or spouse has ceased to occupy ... within the minimum occupation period;
-- (b) ... has at any time acquired ... any title to, or an estate or interest
-- in, any flat, house, building or land; (c) the housing accommodation has been
-- used otherwise than as a housing accommodation within the minimum occupation
-- period; (d) ... assigned, underlet or parted with possession ... within the
-- minimum occupation period without the Minister's prior written consent;
-- (e) ... failed to perform or observe any term or condition ... AFTER the
-- Board or the developer has served ... a written notice ...; (f) ... made a
-- misleading or false statement in his or her application ...; (g) ... made a
-- misrepresentation of a material fact, whether innocently or otherwise ...;
-- (h) ... has contravened section 7(1)(b); or (i) ... has, within the minimum
-- occupation period, ceased to be a citizen of Singapore".
--
-- Nine grounds, any one of which opens the power. The power is "may", so what
-- is decided is whether it ARISES, not whether it is exercised.
DECLARE AcquisitionGrounds HAS
    `ceased to occupy within the minimum occupation period`                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `acquired title to or an interest in any flat, house, building or land`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `used otherwise than as a housing accommodation within the minimum occupation period` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `assigned, underlet or parted with possession within the minimum occupation period without consent` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
    `failed to perform a term or condition after written notice drawing attention to it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
    `made a misleading or false statement in the application`                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)
    `made a misrepresentation of a material fact, whether innocently or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (g)
    `contravened section 7(1)(b)`                                               IS A BOOLEAN   -- (h)
    `ceased to be a citizen of Singapore within the minimum occupation period`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- (i)
    -- s 9(10): the same commercial-property saving as s 5(9), but applied only
    -- to limb (b). Word for word the same test: commercial property acquired
    -- with the Minister's prior written consent, not exceeding $250,000 or such
    -- higher value as the Minister may allow.
    `the property acquired is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars`  IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister has allowed a higher value for this acquisition`              IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(10): "Subsection (1)(b) does not apply to a purchaser ... who has
-- purchased or acquired, with the Minister's prior written consent, any
-- commercial property not exceeding $250,000 in value, or such higher value as
-- the Minister may allow, at the time of purchase."
GIVEN `the grounds` IS AN AcquisitionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 9(10) saving applies` IF
        `the grounds`'s `the property acquired is commercial property acquired with the Minister's prior written consent`
    AND `the acquisition value is within the cap` `the grounds`

GIVEN `the grounds` IS AN AcquisitionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the acquisition value is within the cap` IF
        `the grounds`'s `the value of that commercial property at the time of purchase in dollars`
            AT MOST `the commercial property value cap in dollars`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `the Minister has allowed a higher value for this acquisition`

-- Limb (b) as it actually operates, with s 9(10) read in.
GIVEN `the grounds` IS AN AcquisitionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(1)(b) is made out` IF
        `the grounds`'s `acquired title to or an interest in any flat, house, building or land`
    AND NOT `the section 9(10) saving applies` `the grounds`

GIVEN `the grounds` IS AN AcquisitionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground in section 9(1) is made out` IF
        `the grounds`'s `ceased to occupy within the minimum occupation period`
    ..  `section 9(1)(b) is made out` `the grounds`
    ..  `the grounds`'s `used otherwise than as a housing accommodation within the minimum occupation period`
    ..  `the grounds`'s `assigned, underlet or parted with possession within the minimum occupation period without consent`
    ..  `the grounds`'s `failed to perform a term or condition after written notice drawing attention to it`
    ..  `the grounds`'s `made a misleading or false statement in the application`
    ..  `the grounds`'s `made a misrepresentation of a material fact, whether innocently or otherwise`
    ..  `the grounds`'s `contravened section 7(1)(b)`
    OR  `the grounds`'s `ceased to be a citizen of Singapore within the minimum occupation period`

GIVEN `the grounds` IS AN AcquisitionGrounds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may direct compulsory acquisition` IF
    `a ground in section 9(1) is made out` `the grounds`
